WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-24, with W17 (0.2.3)


STATE

  Version 0.2.3, Phase P3 IN PROGRESS (line editor, history, job
  control, and completion complete), on branch dev. 0.2.3 adds:
  - context-aware completion in include/tam-clam/complete.h and
    src/complete/complete.c: commands (builtins, aliases, functions,
    PATH), files/directories, variables ($VAR/${VAR}), user names
    (~user/), and lazy declarative *.comp files for options/subcommands;
  - starter share/completions/{tam-clam,git,ls,grep,cd}.comp installed
    by make install;
  - Tab (complete-next), Shift+Tab (complete-prev), longest-common-
    prefix expansion, candidate overlay, and Escape restore in
    src/edit/edit.c;
  - tests/test_complete.c unit tests, live PTY completion tests in
    tests/pty/test_pty.c, and sandbox/demo-0.2.3-complete.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  arch/keys.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default.


